/*
  Português do Brasil — partial on purpose (#161).

  Covers the popover, the status and counts lines, the menu-bar item's spoken label, the
  notifications, the welcome window and the reader's empty states: the surfaces
  the acceptance check reads, plus the ones a user meets before anything else. Most of Settings
  is still English here, and falls back to its key, which is the English sentence — that fallback
  is the whole point of the mechanism and this file is where you can watch it work, one row at a
  time. A surface is translated whole or not at all, though: half a pane in each language is the
  one outcome worse than all of it in English.

  Add the missing keys by copying them out of ../en.lproj/Localizable.strings; nothing breaks
  while they are absent. See CONTRIBUTING.md → "Add a language".
*/

